ts=2026-11-17T05:29:23.850Z action=deleted original_ts=2026-11-17T01:15:03.907Z type=blocker scope=figma-mcp content="As of 17 Nov 2026 the Figma MCP is unusable for MberX work: (1) read tools (search_design_system, get_metadata, get_screenshot, use_figma reads) fail with 'You've reached the Figma MCP tool call limit on the Starter plan' — MberX team seat is View on Starter = 20 tool calls/month, exhausted; (2) write path also fails: create_new_file returns 'Looks like you don't have edit access to this file' on every team tried (MberX, HJD, JHCD) although it worked earlier the same day. whoami (exempt) works. Recovery options: upgrade MberX seat to Full + plan to Professional (200/day), or wait for the monthly reset (~1 Dec 2026). Note: figma tools are NOT exposed in opencode code-mode tool registry; they are reachable via direct MCP calls to https://mcp.figma.com/mcp using the OAuth credential in ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db (helper: /private/var/folders/vx/_cxsxg312md095r98v275lpm0000gn/T/opencode/figma-mcp.py)." reason="Resolved by the user on 17 Nov 2026; calls to the Figma MCP now work, so the stale blocker would wrongly stop future builds." tags=figma,mcp,rate-limit,blocker,tipping.spec
